  "worked_solution": "Let us call $x$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{58}^{∘}+x+{65}^{∘}+{63}^{∘}+{97}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{283}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={77}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
